<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Jun (Pengzu)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">252–314</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Jun, courtesy name Pengzu, was a Western Jin governor and general who controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/youzhou">Youzhou</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in the early 4th century. Allied by marriage with the Duan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, he used Duan and Wuhuan cavalry against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-zhao">Han Zhao</a> state founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>. In 314 he was captured and executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-le">Shi Le</a>, the future founder of Later Zhao, who had feigned submission to him.</p></div>
